<p>Use this menu to adjust the advanced settings that can affect the output 
 quality of the print jobs.</p>
<p>Available functions differ depending on the printer or printer driver 
 you are using.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="default" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Restore Defaults</span></p>
<p>Restores the settings on this menu to the default settings.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="cmyk" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Separate into CMYK, then Print in Designated 
 Color Only</span></p>
<p>Normally full color (CMYK) is used for color printing. However, you 
 can choose to use only specific CMYK color(s).</p>
<p><a href="~/Topics/PS_CS/IDH_HOW_CMYK">Printing a Document Using Only Specific 
 CMYK Colors</a></p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="rastervector" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Vector/Raster:</span></p>
<p>Specify how document data are printed. The printer driver can send document 
 data as either raster or vector graphic images. All data can be printed 
 as raster images, but most geometric shapes and patterns print faster 
 as vector images.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Vector</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Sends document data to the printer as a mixture 
 of vector and raster images.</p>
<p class="Note-indent">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p class="Normal-indent">Not all images 
 can be printed using Vector. If you select <span class="Term-Soft">Vector</span> 
 and the images do not print as they appear on the computer screen, select 
 <span class="Term-Soft">Raster</span> and reprint the document.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Raster</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Sends all document data to the printer as raster 
 images.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="thicker" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Line Width Adjustment</span></p>
<p>This function adjusts the thickness of the lines, such as in figures, 
 in dot units.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="textblack" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Print All Text as Black</span></p>
<p>Prints all text in the print job in black regardless of the original 
 color.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="blackover" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Black Over Print</span></p>
<p>This function allows black printing on a colored background and helps 
 prevent misregistration. Use this function if your document features black 
 graphics and/or text on a colored background.</p>
<p><a href="~/Topics/IDH_HOW_BLACK_PRINTING#blackover">Overprinting Black on 
 a Background Color (Black over print)</a></p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="photograph" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Adjust Photographs</span></p>
<p>Corrects the color tone of images taken with a digital camera.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="edgesmooth" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Edge Smoothing</span></p>
<p>Improves the quality of text and graphics by smoothing jagged outer 
 edges to enhance the appearance of curved lines. If you are printing a 
 document that features images containing fine gradations of tone such 
 as photographs, leave this check box unselected.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="fuesr" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Fuser Setting:</span></p>
<p>If residual gloss appears on the same page or the next page, select 
 <span class="Term-Soft">High Quality</span>.</p>
<p><span class="Term-Soft">High Quality</span> may reduce productivity. If 
 residual gloss does not appear, select <span class="Term-Soft">Normal</span>. 
 </p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="dataprocess" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Change Data Processing</span></p>
<p>Depending on the application, there may be cases where printing takes 
 a long time, or colors are not reproduced correctly. In this kind of situation, 
 selecting this may rectify the problem.</p>
<p>Since selecting this may cause printing not to function correctly with 
 some applications, you should normally leave this option unselected.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="ditherbrush" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Shift Shading Pattern</span></p>
<p>Select the check box if the shading pattern appears faint when printing 
 is performed.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="enlargeditherbrush" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Enlarge Shading Pattern</span></p>
<p>Select the check box if the pattern colors are not printed correctly 
 as the dithering and brush effects interfere. </p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="boldtext" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Bold Text Adjustment</span></p>
<p>Prints bold-faced characters even bolder.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="textthick" role="heading">Make Text Thick</p>
<p>This function increases the thickness of the font to be printed by 1 
 dot.</p>
